From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 0099] 0099: pram into the kernel L1's unused L2 slot 1 -
 never touch the L1 descriptor

QEMU r33 (db27350) faulted at arm_vm_init+0xc5c (post-TTBR1-switch, inside
the relocated pram block): its first fresh kernel-image access died with an
L2 translation fault.  Root cause: pram_va 0xfffffe0105dc0000 lives in the
kernel's own L1 slot 2016 (VM_MIN+4.4GB = L2 slot 130), so 0096/0098's
"*l1_tte = new table descriptor" REPLACED the kernel image's L1 entry with
a bare, empty L2 table.  The final tables then had no kernel image at all;
execution survived only on stale TLB entries until the first DTLB miss.

Fix: park the pram at VM_MIN+0x2000000 (L2 slot 1 of the kernel L1 entry -
the window reserved above the low globals, excluded from VM allocation,
measured EMPTY) and write the L3-table pointer through the existing L2
table.  The L1 entry is now read, never written.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
index e8e02b3..fc3de2a 100644
--- a/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
+++ b/osfmk/arm64/arm_vm_init.c
@@ -2220,24 +2220,36 @@ arm_vm_init(uint64_t memory_size, boot_args * args)
 	 * outside the physmap aperture and outside phystokv's range, and
 	 * check_for_panic_log's ml_io_map runs too late to help
 	 * (PE_init_panicheader faulted on platina: boot #25 QEMU nested
-	 * panic).  Map it by hand at a fixed VA in a free L1 slot of the
-	 * final tables.  This MUST run after the TTBR1 switch: pre-switch
-	 * alloc_ptpage's phystokv resolves through the slid physmap window,
-	 * which the still-running bootstrap tables do not map (QEMU r31:
-	 * bzero fault at _bzero+0x1c; r32: the same class at
-	 * arm_vm_init+0xbe4).  Post-switch cpu_tte's physmap L1/L2 carry
-	 * the window, so phystokv works normally here. */
+	 * panic).  Map it by hand at a fixed VA in the unused 32MB L2 slot
+	 * right above the low globals (VM_MIN+32..64MB): that window is
+	 * reserved and excluded from VM allocation, and measured EMPTY in
+	 * the final tables.  Write the L3-table pointer through the
+	 * kernel's EXISTING L1 entry - never touch the L1 descriptor
+	 * itself: the whole kernel VA space is one L1 slot, and 0096/0098's
+	 * pram_va (VM_MIN+4.4GB, same slot, L2 slot 130) made the old
+	 * fresh-L1 write unhook the kernel image from the final tables
+	 * (QEMU r33: first fresh kernel-image access L2-faults at
+	 * arm_vm_init+0xc5c).  This MUST run after the TTBR1 switch:
+	 * pre-switch alloc_ptpage's phystokv resolves through the slid
+	 * physmap window, which the running bootstrap tables do not map
+	 * (QEMU r31: bzero fault at _bzero+0x1c; r32: arm_vm_init+0xbe4). */
 	{
-		vm_map_address_t pram_va = (vm_map_address_t)0xfffffe0105dc0000ULL;
+		vm_map_address_t pram_va = (vm_map_address_t)0xfffffe0002000000ULL;
 		pmap_paddr_t pram_pa = args->physBase + args->memSize;
-		vm_offset_t l2page = alloc_ptpage(TRUE);
 		tt_entry_t *l1_tte = cpu_tte + ((pram_va & ARM_TT_L1_INDEX_MASK) >> ARM_TT_L1_SHIFT);
-		pt_entry_t *l3 = (pt_entry_t *)l2page;
+		tt_entry_t *l2_tte;
+		pt_entry_t *l3;
 		uint32_t i;
 
-		*l1_tte = (kvtophys(l2page) & ARM_TTE_TABLE_MASK) |
+		assert((*l1_tte & (ARM_TTE_VALID | ARM_TTE_TYPE_MASK)) ==
+		    (ARM_TTE_VALID | ARM_TTE_TYPE_TABLE));
+		l2_tte = (tt_entry_t *)phystokv(*l1_tte & ARM_TTE_TABLE_MASK) +
+		    ((pram_va & ARM_TT_L2_INDEX_MASK) >> ARM_TT_L2_SHIFT);
+		assert(*l2_tte == ARM_TTE_EMPTY);
+		l3 = (pt_entry_t *)alloc_ptpage(TRUE);
+		*l2_tte = (kvtophys((vm_offset_t)l3) & ARM_TTE_TABLE_MASK) |
 		    ARM_TTE_TYPE_TABLE | ARM_TTE_VALID;
-		bzero((void *)l2page, ARM_PGBYTES);
+		bzero((void *)l3, ARM_PGBYTES);
 		for (i = 0; i < (0x1000000 / ARM_PGBYTES); i++) {
 			l3[i] = (pram_pa + (uint64_t)i * ARM_PGBYTES) |
 			    ARM_PTE_TYPE |
